{"id": "cb9175f0-6d94-41ca-8fa8-595a653c42e3", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "This PR doesn't add anything to the AWS bill.

Looking at the changed files: it's a code-only change — adding exponential backoff retry logic to the DynamoDB client and a new `RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5` setting, plus tests and a README update. No infrastructure-as-code files (CloudFormation, CDK, Terraform, SAM templates) were touched, so no new resources, capacity, or configuration changes are being provisioned.

One thing worth flagging functionally (not cost-wise): more retries with backoff *could* marginally increase DynamoDB request volume during throttling events, since failed requests get retried instead of failing fast. But that's usage-pattern noise under error conditions, not a billing line item from the PR itself — and it's just as likely to reduce costly downstream failures/timeouts instead.", "type": "text"}], "created_at": null}

